WEBVTT

00:50.383 --> 00:52.552
DOONA!

01:19.370 --> 01:20.580
Would you let me go?

01:23.583 --> 01:27.087
What kind of question is that?
You should go if you want to.

01:28.088 --> 01:29.798
But I think it would be nice.

01:32.008 --> 01:33.635
I want to see you sing.

01:34.761 --> 01:36.930
I like that you're a fool.

01:42.811 --> 01:44.729
What if they tell me to break up with you?

01:45.688 --> 01:46.773
Should I still go back?

01:48.650 --> 01:50.819
Given all this, neither the company

01:50.902 --> 01:52.862
nor Doona is stupid enough

01:52.946 --> 01:55.198
to take on the risk of a relationship.

01:58.243 --> 02:01.079
So, who should be the one
to let her go? Me?

02:23.935 --> 02:25.353
EPISODE 9
DOONA!

02:25.436 --> 02:26.563
LEE DOONA SOLO ALBUM

02:26.646 --> 02:27.856
Congratulations!

02:31.192 --> 02:32.694
CONGRATS ON THE COMEBACK!

02:32.777 --> 02:35.989
ALL OF MSA WISHES YOU SUCCESS
IN YOUR SOLO CAREER, DOONA!

02:44.038 --> 02:47.792
FROZEN WATER PIPE PREVENTION TIPS

02:55.008 --> 02:57.802
I've moved. I'll leave you my new address.

03:00.180 --> 03:03.224
It's getting colder now. Are you well?

03:03.308 --> 03:05.226
RECRUITMENT
GENERAL CIVIL ENGINEERING

03:07.687 --> 03:09.772
We don't have any photos together.

03:10.481 --> 03:12.483
Let's take some when we have time.

03:12.567 --> 03:13.693
EXAM SCHEDULE

03:21.910 --> 03:23.453
You're pretty!

03:23.536 --> 03:24.579
You're so pretty!

03:24.662 --> 03:25.788
I love you!

03:26.331 --> 03:27.290
Doona!

03:27.373 --> 03:28.750
Look over here, please!

03:29.375 --> 03:31.878
- You're so pretty!
- You're so pretty!

03:31.961 --> 03:32.962
- Hello.
- Hello.

03:33.046 --> 03:34.672
Here. I brought you a gift.

03:34.756 --> 03:37.217
- Thank you.
- You're so pretty!

03:38.426 --> 03:40.178
I like your glasses.

03:40.261 --> 03:42.055
Would you mind if I tried them on?

03:43.514 --> 03:45.016
Where do they sell these things?

03:47.393 --> 03:49.979
Could you find out
where you can get these?

03:50.063 --> 03:52.607
And escort this gentleman out, please.

03:54.025 --> 03:55.318
Security, please.

03:59.447 --> 04:01.115
So disappointed.

04:03.868 --> 04:06.996
IT'S SMOOTH ENOUGH
TO DOWN IN ONE GO!

04:13.044 --> 04:15.004
You must be very shy.

04:16.297 --> 04:17.382
Hello, Doona.

04:27.433 --> 04:29.143
Wait, is this…

04:35.191 --> 04:36.442
No, it can't be.

04:39.821 --> 04:41.864
TO SU-JIN FROM DOONA
GO, KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE!

04:51.040 --> 04:55.003
MINSONG TOGETHER FESTIVAL
OUTDOOR CONCERT, LEE DOONA

04:55.086 --> 04:57.338
I'm so busy preparing
for the end of the semester.

05:07.890 --> 05:09.142
I miss you.

05:26.409 --> 05:29.996
It feels like
we are in different universes.

05:37.253 --> 05:39.672
The others are over there
drinking more. Let's go too.

05:39.756 --> 05:41.591
- Sure, let's go.
- They should be…

05:41.674 --> 05:42.967
- My God.
- She's so pretty.

05:43.051 --> 05:44.886
How can her face be so tiny?

05:52.894 --> 05:54.395
And we're sitting

05:55.605 --> 05:57.899
side by side at the same station
purely by chance.

06:00.193 --> 06:02.195
Yes. We've just finished up
and headed out.

06:03.196 --> 06:04.113
About an hour?

06:05.782 --> 06:07.158
The article is in two days.

06:07.241 --> 06:09.285
It's all been confirmed
with the Japan team,

06:09.369 --> 06:10.703
so keep it confidential till then.

06:34.977 --> 06:36.604
I feel angry today somehow.

06:47.949 --> 06:49.534
CRAM SCHOOL

06:51.828 --> 06:52.912
It's snowing.

06:53.955 --> 06:55.873
It's the end of the semester
in a few days.

06:58.376 --> 07:00.670
My part-time job
at the cram school is ending too.

07:31.868 --> 07:34.787
It's cold out, but I haven't seen
the stray cat Nana around.

07:35.663 --> 07:37.582
I'd better look for her tonight.

08:21.792 --> 08:22.668
Are you done?

08:24.629 --> 08:26.005
Let's go get something to eat.

08:38.518 --> 08:39.519
Cheers.

08:47.652 --> 08:49.278
You called me a lot, right?

08:50.029 --> 08:50.863
No.

08:53.241 --> 08:54.116
Really?

08:55.785 --> 08:59.580
I thought you'd have been worried
about me. I'm glad you weren't.

09:09.215 --> 09:11.509
I couldn't use my phone.

09:12.510 --> 09:14.470
I barely managed to get out now as it is.

09:17.848 --> 09:21.227
I understand.
You don't have to explain anything.

09:22.353 --> 09:25.356
You were made for the stage.

09:29.193 --> 09:30.319
I'll be rooting for you.

09:38.327 --> 09:39.245
Everything's…

09:41.330 --> 09:42.748
okay between us, right?

09:46.711 --> 09:48.004
I'm off to the military.

09:53.968 --> 09:54.969
Yeah?

10:00.850 --> 10:01.809
That's good.

10:02.310 --> 10:04.145
At least the time will pass quickly.

10:15.531 --> 10:17.783
The agency treats me like a crazy woman.

10:18.993 --> 10:20.620
They won't let me use a phone,

10:20.703 --> 10:22.872
and someone even follows me
to the bathroom.

10:22.955 --> 10:24.999
They must be scared I'll run away again.

10:25.833 --> 10:27.293
They really don't have to.

10:30.171 --> 10:32.506
This is what prior convictions
get you, right?

10:55.029 --> 10:59.533
Given the situation,
I have to be careful for the time being,

11:00.409 --> 11:01.994
but it will be two years max.

11:03.079 --> 11:06.374
Once I'm established, my private life
won't be much of an issue anymore.

11:07.625 --> 11:08.584
And then--

11:08.668 --> 11:09.919
You don't…

11:17.635 --> 11:19.261
You don't have to worry about me.

11:35.027 --> 11:38.280
You want to end things here?
Is that what you're saying?

11:39.407 --> 11:40.700
Were you saying something else?

11:42.326 --> 11:43.911
I was saying something else.

11:49.792 --> 11:51.043
That's what I was saying.

11:54.797 --> 11:56.215
I want to stop here.

12:28.289 --> 12:31.500
When I was a washed-up has-been
with nothing going on in my life,

12:31.584 --> 12:33.961
you thought you had a shot
at playing around with me,

12:34.044 --> 12:36.297
but now that I've gone back,
you can't handle it?

12:39.008 --> 12:40.760
Do you know what I did when I met him?

12:41.677 --> 12:43.637
I told him I was going to date you!

12:44.513 --> 12:46.724
I told him
I was going to keep dating you, so…

12:52.229 --> 12:54.190
It's true. I want it all.

12:55.524 --> 12:57.818
That's why
it really hasn't been easy for me.

13:00.905 --> 13:03.032
So, why is it so easy for you?

13:04.200 --> 13:06.494
What is it
that I've been trying to endure for us?

13:08.078 --> 13:09.789
What are you enduring for us?

13:11.248 --> 13:12.166
Tell me.

13:12.917 --> 13:15.127
You said I should go if I wanted to.

13:16.420 --> 13:18.631
You said you wanted to see me sing!

13:32.186 --> 13:33.771
And you're the one who let go.

13:35.314 --> 13:37.525
You're the one
who's breaking your promise.

13:38.025 --> 13:40.778
You're the one running away
because you don't have the guts.

13:41.695 --> 13:43.531
And you're the one who's discarding me.

13:46.158 --> 13:47.868
Just like all the others.

13:51.580 --> 13:52.581
Is that it?

13:56.585 --> 13:57.461
Is that it?

14:04.176 --> 14:05.177
Yes.

17:04.273 --> 17:05.274
That's good.

17:09.695 --> 17:10.738
Action!

18:13.008 --> 18:13.842
I'VE MOVED

18:13.926 --> 18:14.760
I MISS YOU

18:14.843 --> 18:16.762
IT FEELS LIKE
WE ARE IN DIFFERENT UNIVERSES

18:16.845 --> 18:19.807
AND WE'RE SITTING SIDE BY SIDE
AT THE SAME STATION PURELY BY CHANCE

18:27.940 --> 18:29.108
What is dating?

18:29.942 --> 18:31.735
Dating is a muscle.

18:41.120 --> 18:42.538
What do you think, everyone?

18:42.621 --> 18:45.749
We've all been broken
at some point in our lives, right?

18:46.416 --> 18:49.294
Being broken and feeling pain is necessary

18:49.378 --> 18:51.213
for building muscle.

18:51.296 --> 18:52.506
"IS IT OKAY TO LOVE AGAIN?"

18:52.589 --> 18:54.591
That's how we get stronger.

18:54.675 --> 18:56.844
DATING = MUSCLE

18:56.927 --> 18:58.846
Bulking up your heart!

18:59.763 --> 19:02.057
Bulking up…

19:03.016 --> 19:05.060
Bulking up your heart.

19:05.644 --> 19:07.771
Tell me, everyone. What is dating again?

19:07.855 --> 19:09.189
It's a muscle.

19:09.273 --> 19:11.441
Not loud enough. What is dating?

19:11.525 --> 19:12.526
It's a muscle!

19:12.609 --> 19:13.944
What is dating?

19:14.027 --> 19:14.987
It's a muscle!

19:15.070 --> 19:16.530
One last time. What is dating?

19:16.613 --> 19:18.699
- It's a muscle!
- It's a muscle!

19:18.782 --> 19:21.827
You can do it!
We can all have a love life!

19:21.910 --> 19:23.662
All we have to do is bulk up!

19:24.538 --> 19:25.539
Like this.

19:25.622 --> 19:28.959
Let's bulk up for love!

19:29.042 --> 19:30.294
Seo Yun-taek!

19:52.107 --> 19:53.442
- Hey!
- Yeah.

19:53.942 --> 19:54.818
Hey!

20:00.741 --> 20:03.619
Get up and have breakfast.
I have to go to work.

20:11.001 --> 20:13.253
- Come on.
- Okay.

20:37.861 --> 20:39.029
I'm off to work.

20:41.156 --> 20:43.450
You're up early,
given how much you had last night.

20:43.533 --> 20:45.953
Yeah, I was planning to go home
and sleep, but…

20:46.036 --> 20:49.039
I'll do that. You should at least
have a protein bar or something.

20:53.377 --> 20:55.504
Here you go. And you.

20:57.214 --> 20:58.840
- Don't forget to take this.
- Thanks.

21:01.051 --> 21:02.761
- I'm off.
- See you later.

21:04.721 --> 21:05.806
Bye.

21:08.725 --> 21:10.686
The job seems to be going
all right for her.

21:11.186 --> 21:14.231
Such a surprise. I never thought
I-ra would have a desk job.

21:14.314 --> 21:16.024
It's weirder I'm living with a woman.

21:16.608 --> 21:17.734
That's true.

21:18.777 --> 21:20.487
I still can't get used to it.

21:22.322 --> 21:23.991
I gotta get to work. Take your time.

21:24.074 --> 21:25.075
- Thanks.
- Sure.

21:40.424 --> 21:41.883
- Won-jun.
- Won-jun.

21:41.967 --> 21:42.801
Hey.

21:43.343 --> 21:45.762
- Hello.
- Hello.

21:54.730 --> 21:56.857
HANG IN THERE!
MAYBE DREAM SWEET WILL VISIT?

21:56.940 --> 21:59.067
TO SU-JIN FROM DOONA
GO, KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE!

22:08.076 --> 22:11.163
The Oseong Apartment people are saying
they asked for pickled ginger.

22:11.747 --> 22:13.498
- They want it delivered now.
- What?

22:15.375 --> 22:17.419
What are they talking about?
It's not there.

22:23.383 --> 22:27.512
Hello. I'm calling
from Su-jin's Seafood House.

22:27.596 --> 22:30.724
The pickled ginger has to be ordered
as a menu item.

22:35.228 --> 22:36.980
Yes, thank you.

22:38.440 --> 22:39.900
- I'll go drop it off.
- Won-jun.

22:39.983 --> 22:42.402
I think they're doing this
because you look easy.

22:42.486 --> 22:43.737
I'll go myself.

22:43.820 --> 22:44.988
No, I'll do it.

22:45.072 --> 22:48.200
I'm going.
You just hang out with Jin-ju here.

22:49.076 --> 22:50.077
With who?

22:50.702 --> 22:51.536
With me.

22:57.167 --> 22:59.836
I was glaring at you,
wondering when you would notice me.

22:59.920 --> 23:01.463
You couldn't feel it?

23:02.339 --> 23:03.799
When did you come back to Korea?

23:06.802 --> 23:07.886
Have a seat first.

23:09.638 --> 23:12.891
This is the desert in Las Vegas.
Look at this.

23:12.974 --> 23:14.226
What are they? Rocks?

23:14.309 --> 23:16.103
Yes. Aren't they pretty?

23:16.186 --> 23:19.689
- Wow, that's amazing.
- This is Times Square in the States.

23:19.773 --> 23:22.818
I recognize it.
It's that famous New Year's spot, right?

23:22.901 --> 23:25.695
- Yes, that's exactly it.
- I wish I could go.

23:26.196 --> 23:27.739
These are my Brazilian friends.

23:28.448 --> 23:30.534
Look. This guy is a photographer.

23:30.617 --> 23:32.202
He takes amazing photos.

23:32.911 --> 23:34.538
He's a good-looking dude.

23:35.372 --> 23:37.290
This was taken on my way to school.

23:37.374 --> 23:39.626
This restaurant is
right across from where I live.

23:39.709 --> 23:41.920
I literally go there every day.
The food is great.

23:42.003 --> 23:43.380
- It's called Habibi?
- Yes.

23:44.881 --> 23:48.260
- Isn't the weather in Brazil amazing?
- It looks awesome.

23:49.177 --> 23:52.305
- Look at this.
- Wow. That looks amazing.

23:52.389 --> 23:53.974
God, I so want to go.

23:54.641 --> 23:57.144
- I'm going to go clean up. Keep talking.
- Okay.

23:57.811 --> 23:59.604
This is I-ra's parents' place.

23:59.688 --> 24:03.608
It's impossible to find a place to live
in Brazil, so I'm doing a homestay here.

24:03.692 --> 24:06.653
I went to visit in the summer
and then just ended up staying on.

24:09.030 --> 24:09.906
Oh no.

24:16.955 --> 24:19.624
Doona also happened to be
in Brazil for a concert.

24:23.837 --> 24:25.255
Where are you going now?

24:25.338 --> 24:29.134
Oh, to my sister's.
She's coming to pick me up after work.

24:29.217 --> 24:30.218
Right.

24:43.523 --> 24:48.945
SU-JIN'S SEAFOOD HOUSE (DELIVERY-ONLY)

25:32.322 --> 25:35.158
CONGRATS ON 4-YEAR ANNIVERSARY
OF YOUR DEBUT AS A SOLO ARTIST!

26:16.491 --> 26:19.619
AEIHERUMUH
LOVE AND DO WHAT YOU WILL

26:33.049 --> 26:35.510
So, is this house going to be demolished?

26:36.344 --> 26:37.220
The house?

26:38.305 --> 26:41.516
It'll still be around.
The landlady's son is getting married,

26:41.600 --> 26:44.561
so she's renovating it
and gifting it as their marital home.

26:45.520 --> 26:47.439
Whoever the guy is, I'm so jealous of him.

26:47.522 --> 26:51.568
Does that mean this is the last time
we're getting together here like this?

26:51.651 --> 26:53.278
That's a bit sad!

26:53.361 --> 26:54.696
Yeah, it is.

26:55.196 --> 26:57.449
Hey, it's been ages
since we all got together, so…

26:58.783 --> 27:00.368
Oh! We're missing Doona.

27:01.244 --> 27:03.455
Doona has to be here for our family

27:03.538 --> 27:06.583
to be reunited in its entirety. Doona--

27:06.666 --> 27:09.586
Eat your veggies
if you want to be healthy!

27:10.170 --> 27:11.671
Let's toast to health!

27:11.755 --> 27:13.131
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

27:13.214 --> 27:14.049
Cheers!

27:20.847 --> 27:22.265
Why aren't you drinking?

27:22.349 --> 27:24.559
- I have an interview tomorrow.
- What interview?

27:27.729 --> 27:28.938
I passed the second stage.

27:30.357 --> 27:31.191
No way!

27:31.733 --> 27:35.278
- Dude! Lee Won-jun!
- Won-jun!

27:35.362 --> 27:39.157
Congratulations! That's my boy!

27:39.240 --> 27:42.619
Seriously, it's such a waste
to leave you single!

27:42.702 --> 27:44.496
Why didn't you tell us sooner?

27:47.666 --> 27:49.834
Really, you never change, do you?

27:49.918 --> 27:53.338
Always keeping things to yourself.
I'd like to see what's inside you.

27:53.963 --> 27:56.716
- I'll tell you when I get the job.
- That will be too late.

27:58.551 --> 27:59.928
I'll tell you even if I fail.

28:01.012 --> 28:03.181
- Knock on wood! Don't jinx it!
- Knock on wood.

28:03.264 --> 28:05.767
- Knock on wood!
- Good luck, Won-jun! And congrats!

28:05.850 --> 28:07.894
- Congratulations!
- Cheers!

28:07.977 --> 28:10.063
It's been ages
since we've had Jin-ju with us.

28:10.146 --> 28:12.023
- Let's continue at our place!
- I-ra.

28:12.107 --> 28:14.150
- You're a traitor if you bail.
- Get in.

28:14.234 --> 28:15.860
- My interview.
- Just one more drink.

28:15.944 --> 28:17.946
Jin-ju, in front.
Won-jun, you're not coming?

28:18.029 --> 28:19.531
- He has an interview.
- That sucks.

28:19.614 --> 28:21.199
- Get in.
- Call us when you get it.

28:21.282 --> 28:23.535
- Okay. Take care.
- Won-jun, get that job!

28:23.618 --> 28:25.662
- Take care.
- Won-jun!

28:25.745 --> 28:27.038
- You're a traitor!
- Bye!

28:27.122 --> 28:28.456
Quiet!

30:51.057 --> 30:51.933
Hello.

30:56.813 --> 30:58.439
I thought you had left.

31:00.024 --> 31:01.234
I left my jacket here.

31:02.735 --> 31:04.821
Then go and get it.

32:00.043 --> 32:02.754
- How's everyone? Are they well?
- Yeah.

32:09.719 --> 32:10.595
They're well.

32:14.265 --> 32:15.767
Have you listened to my music?

33:29.382 --> 33:30.299
Lee Won-jun!

33:32.051 --> 33:33.052
Won-jun!

33:40.518 --> 33:41.769
"Take care"?

33:42.770 --> 33:45.314
- Is that all you have to say to me?
- Yes, it is.

33:48.151 --> 33:49.360
Let's talk inside.

34:06.794 --> 34:10.298
- How can you be so calm?
- Is that how it looks to you?

34:11.257 --> 34:14.927
Do you know what you were to me back then?

34:16.721 --> 34:19.057
If it weren't for you,
I wouldn't be alive now.

34:19.557 --> 34:20.767
Because at the time,

34:22.143 --> 34:26.147
I despised myself so much,
I didn't want to wake up each day.

34:27.065 --> 34:30.401
I didn't care about what tomorrow held.
It was only because of you--

34:30.485 --> 34:32.278
Things are different now.

34:33.446 --> 34:37.158
You're right. They are different.
Because I really like myself now.

34:37.909 --> 34:39.494
I'm better than I've ever been.

34:39.577 --> 34:43.623
I'm not lonely, I'm not hurting,
I sleep well, my work is going well,

34:44.290 --> 34:46.626
and I have many people
by my side even without you.

34:48.628 --> 34:49.837
So now,

34:50.463 --> 34:52.006
I no longer need you.

34:54.133 --> 34:55.134
I know.

35:02.225 --> 35:04.352
So this time, it's your turn to beg.

35:06.771 --> 35:07.730
Tell me you're sorry.

35:09.649 --> 35:11.192
Tell me you did me wrong.

35:16.072 --> 35:17.031
I'm sorry.

35:18.741 --> 35:20.159
I did you wrong.

35:21.702 --> 35:22.870
Tell me you regret it.

35:24.288 --> 35:25.832
Tell me you regretted it!

35:31.462 --> 35:32.630
I regret it.

35:35.341 --> 35:37.093
I regret it every single day.

35:39.011 --> 35:40.972
So please leave me in peace now!

35:43.599 --> 35:44.475
Please.

35:48.479 --> 35:49.772
I've missed you.

36:00.366 --> 36:01.826
I've missed you too.

36:22.305 --> 36:25.433
2027 NATIONAL CIVIL SERVANT LEVEL 5
OPEN COMPETITIVE RECRUITMENT EXAM

36:27.518 --> 36:29.854
LEE WON-JUN

38:27.888 --> 38:28.723
LEE DOONA

38:28.806 --> 38:29.765
YOU'RE AWESOME, DOONA

38:30.975 --> 38:32.143
Doona!

38:36.272 --> 38:37.356
I love you, Doona!

39:20.649 --> 39:21.984
Here's your card, sir.

39:23.110 --> 39:24.111
Here you go.

39:25.363 --> 39:26.447
Thank you.

39:27.907 --> 39:28.783
Let's go.

39:29.700 --> 39:30.534
Yes, sir.

39:36.457 --> 39:38.209
It's Doona. Did you see her?

39:38.709 --> 39:39.752
So pretty!

39:42.129 --> 39:44.382
Sir, it's this way.

39:45.758 --> 39:46.675
Allow me, please.

41:48.547 --> 41:53.552
Subtitle translation by: Reuben Simpson
